            <h2>Fund Research vs Portfolio Tracking: The Core Distinction</h2>

            <p>Value Research Online is fundamentally a <strong>fund research tool</strong>. Its star ratings, category rankings, portfolio overlap checker, and fund manager history are indispensable when you're deciding <em>which</em> fund to invest in. VRO has built enormous trust over decades by providing unbiased, data-rich fund analysis.</p>

            <p>Arthavi is a <strong>portfolio tracking and analytics tool</strong>. Once you've chosen your funds and invested, Arthavi takes over — tracking what you own, calculating true XIRR from your actual transactions, risk-scoring your portfolio, and delivering AI-powered insights about your specific holdings.</p>

            <p>These are complementary, not competing. Many serious investors use VRO to pick funds and Arthavi to track them — getting the best of both worlds.</p>

            <h2>Where Value Research Falls Short as a Tracker</h2>

            <p>VRO's portfolio tracker exists as a secondary feature — it was built for research, not tracking. Its limitations are significant for active portfolio management:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Manual transaction entry:</strong> VRO's portfolio requires you to enter every SIP transaction by hand. Miss a month and your returns are inaccurate.</li>
                <li><strong>No CAS import:</strong> VRO does not support automatic import from CAMS or KFintech. Arthavi imports your entire history from your investment statement in seconds.</li>
                <li><strong>No AI layer:</strong> VRO offers static fund data. Arthavi lets you ask your portfolio questions: <em>"Am I over-exposed to mid-caps?"</em> or <em>"What is my sectoral concentration?"</em></li>
                <li><strong>No Portfolio Health Score:</strong> VRO rates <em>funds</em>, not your <em>portfolio</em> as a whole. Arthavi combines your holdings into a single 0–100 health score with diversification and risk subscores.</li>
                <li><strong>Desktop-primary UX:</strong> VRO's interface is designed for desktop research. Arthavi is mobile-first with biometric lock, Privacy Mode, and haptic-enabled Smart Insights.</li>
            </ul>

