            <h2>What Value Research Does Well — And Where It Stops</h2>
            <p>VRO is irreplaceable for one thing: deciding <em>which</em> fund to buy. Its rating consistency, portfolio overlap tool, and category comparison are industry-standard. But the moment you've invested, VRO's usefulness drops sharply. It has no CAS import, its portfolio tracker requires full manual data entry, and it has no AI analysis layer whatsoever.</p>
            <p>Most investors who rely on VRO for tracking are unknowingly working with incomplete or stale data — because keeping a manually-entered portfolio current across dozens of SIP transactions requires discipline most people don't maintain.</p>

            <h2>Arthavi Is the Tracking Layer Every VRO User Is Missing</h2>
            <p>Arthavi handles everything VRO doesn't. Import your CAS and your complete transaction history loads instantly — no manual entry. Your XIRR is calculated correctly from the authoritative CAMS/KFintech data, not from memory-based entries. Your Portfolio Health Score, Smart Insights, and Ask AI give you ongoing intelligence that static fund ratings can never provide.</p>
            <p>The right workflow for a serious Indian mutual fund investor is clear: <strong>use Value Research to choose funds, and use Arthavi to track them</strong>. Not as equals — but as a research tool and an analytics platform that together give you the complete picture from fund selection through to real wealth measurement.</p>

